actionMatrix -- matrix of a linearly reductive action
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        actionMatrix L
  * Inputs:
      * L, an instance of the type *note LinearlyReductiveAction:
        LinearlyReductiveAction,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, of a group action on a ring

Description
===========

This function is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,.

Suppose the action L consists of the linearly reductive group with coordinate
ring S/I (where S is a polynomial ring) acting on a (quotient of) a polynomial
ring R via the action matrix M. This function returns the action matrix M.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[z]                                        |
|                                                      |
|o1 = S                                                |
|                                                      |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(z^2 - 1)                               |
|                                                      |
|            2                                         |
|o2 = ideal(z  - 1)                                    |
|                                                      |
|o2 : Ideal of S                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = matrix{{(z+1)/2, (1-z)/2},{(1-z)/2, (z+1)/2}}|
|                                                      |
|o3 = | 1/2z+1/2  -1/2z+1/2 |                          |
|     | -1/2z+1/2 1/2z+1/2  |                          |
|                                                      |
|             2      2                                 |
|o3 : Matrix S  <-- S                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = QQ[x,y]                                      |
|                                                      |
|o4 = R                                                |
|                                                      |
|o4 : PolynomialRing                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : L = linearlyReductiveAction(I, M, R)             |
|                                                      |
|                   2                                  |
|o5 = R <- S/ideal(z  - 1) via                         |
|                                                      |
|     | 1/2z+1/2  -1/2z+1/2 |                          |
|     | -1/2z+1/2 1/2z+1/2  |                          |
|                                                      |
|o5 : LinearlyReductiveAction                          |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : actionMatrix L                                   |
|                                                      |
|o6 = | 1/2z+1/2  -1/2z+1/2 |                          |
|     | -1/2z+1/2 1/2z+1/2  |                          |
|                                                      |
|             2      2                                 |
|o6 : Matrix S  <-- S                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------+

