GroupAction -- the class of all group actions
*********************************************

Description
===========

This class is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,.

GroupAction is the class of all group actions on polynomial rings for the
purpose of computing invariants. This is not typically used directly,
delegating creation to the various constructor functions for different kinds of
group actions:

  * *note FiniteGroupAction: FiniteGroupAction,, the class of a finite matrix
    group action, is created with *note finiteAction: finiteAction,
  * *note DiagonalAction: DiagonalAction,, the class of the diagonal action of
    a product of a torus and a finite abelian group, is created with *note
    diagonalAction: diagonalAction,
  * *note LinearlyReductiveAction: LinearlyReductiveAction,, the class of a
    linearly reductive matrix group action, is created with *note
    linearlyReductiveAction: linearlyReductiveAction,

Each class implements different algorithms to compute invariants. Although
mathematically speaking all the above group actions are linearly reductive (at
least in the non modular case), the class *note LinearlyReductiveAction:
LinearlyReductiveAction, should be used only when none of the other classes
apply because it has fewer and possibly less efficient methods.

The class GroupAction is implemented as a HashTable. When created it stores
information such as the action (in a format dependent upon the group) and the
polynomial ring being acted upon.

Types of GroupAction:
=====================

  * *note DiagonalAction: DiagonalAction, -- the class of all diagonal actions
  * *note FiniteGroupAction: FiniteGroupAction, -- the class of all finite
    group actions
  * *note LinearlyReductiveAction: LinearlyReductiveAction, -- the class of all
    (non finite, non toric) linearly reductive group actions

Functions and methods returning an object of class GroupAction:
===============================================================

  * "action(RingOfInvariants)" -- see *note action: action, -- the group action
    that produced a ring of invariants

Methods that use an object of class GroupAction:
================================================

  * *note dim(GroupAction): dim_lpGroupAction_rp, -- dimension of the
    polynomial ring being acted upon
  * "invariantRing(GroupAction)" -- see *note invariantRing: invariantRing, --
    the ring of invariants of a group action
  * "PolynomialRing ^ GroupAction" -- see *note invariantRing: invariantRing,
    -- the ring of invariants of a group action
  * *note ring(GroupAction): ring_lpGroupAction_rp, -- the polynomial ring
    being acted upon

For the programmer
==================

The object *note GroupAction: GroupAction, is a *note type:
(Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with ancestor classes *note HashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, < *note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

