        secondaryInvariants that determines the printing of an informative
        polynomial
  * Outputs:
      * a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, (P,S), where P is a *note
        List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of primary invariants (i.e. a homogeneous
        system of parameters for the invariant ring) and S is a *note List:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List, of corresponding secondary invariants

Description
===========

This function is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,.

                                                                               
*note hironakaDecomposition: hironakaDecomposition,  makes use of the functions
                                                                               
                                                                          
*note primaryInvariants: primaryInvariants, and *note secondaryInvariants:
                                                                          
                                                                        
secondaryInvariants, in order to compute a Hironaka decomposition of the
                                                                        
                                                                              
invariant ring of a finite group G acting on a polynomial ring R. It outputs a
                                                                              
                                                                            
sequence ({f ,...,f }, {g ,...,g }) of primary and secondary invariants such
            1      n     1      r                                           
      G
that R =Ag $\oplus$...$\oplus$Ag , where A=K[f ,...,f ] and K is the field of
          1                     r             1      n
coefficients of R.

All of the optional arguments of *note hironakaDecomposition:
hironakaDecomposition, play the same role as for the functions *note
primaryInvariants: primaryInvariants, and *note secondaryInvariants:
secondaryInvariants,. By default, the function *note hironakaDecomposition:
hironakaDecomposition, calls upon *note primaryInvariants: primaryInvariants,,
with the optional argument *note Dade:
primaryInvariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDade=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, set to *note false:
(Macaulay2Doc)false,, to compute a set of primary invariants, resulting in
Kemper's 'optimal' algorithm being used (see *note hsop algorithms: hsop
algorithms, for more information).

The example below computes a set of primary and secondary invariants for an
action of the cyclic group of order 4 on QQ[x,y].

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : C4=finiteAction({matrix{{0,-1},{1,0}}},QQ[x,y])|
|                                                    |
|o1 = QQ[x..y] <- <| 0 -1 |>                         |
|                  | 1 0  |                          |
|                                                    |
|o1 : FiniteGroupAction                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : hironakaDecomposition C4                       |
|                                                    |
|        2    2     3       3        4    4          |
|o2 = ({x  + y , - x y + x*y }, {1, x  + y })        |
|                                                    |
|o2 : Sequence                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------+

                                     C4                           4  4        
From the output one sees that QQ[x,y]  =QQ[f f ]$\oplus$QQ[f f ](x +y ), where
                                            1 2             1 2               
    2  2          3  3
f =x +y  and f =xy -x y.
 1            2

Caveat
======

Currently hironakaDecomposition works only with polynomial rings and matrices
over fields of characteristic 0.

