invariants -- computes the generating invariants of a group action
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        invariants G
  * Inputs:
      * G, an instance of the type *note GroupAction: GroupAction,, a specific
        type of group action on a polynomial ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note DegreeBound: invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeBound=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value infinity, degree bound for invariants of finite
        groups
      * *note DegreeLimit: invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value {}, GB option for invariants
      * *note Strategy: invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value "Default", choose the strategy for computing
        invariants
      * *note SubringLimit: invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSubringLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value infinity, GB option for invariants
      * *note UseCoefficientRing:
        invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmUseCoefficientRing=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, option to compute invariants over the given
        coefficient ring
      * *note UsePolyhedra: invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmUsePolyhedra=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value false, use Polyhedra package for invariants of
        tori
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a minimal set of generating
        invariants for the group action

Description
===========

This function is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,. This
function can be used to compute the generating invariants of a diagonal group
action, finite group action or linearly reductive group action. It can also be
used to compute a basis of a graded component of the invariant ring. Below is a
list of the many ways to use this function:

  * *note invariants(FiniteGroupAction): invariants_lpFiniteGroupAction_rp,:
    computes the generating invariants of a finite group action
  * *note invariants(DiagonalAction): invariants_lpDiagonalAction_rp,: computes
    the generating invariants of a diagonal group action
  * *note invariants(LinearlyReductiveAction):
    invariants_lpLinearlyReductiveAction_rp,: computes the generating
    invariants of a linearly reductive action
  * *note invariants(FiniteGroupAction,ZZ):
    invariants_lpFiniteGroupAction_cmZZ_rp, or *note
    invariants(FiniteGroupAction,List):
    invariants_lpFiniteGroupAction_cmZZ_rp,: computes a basis for graded
    component of the invariant ring of a finite group action
  * *note invariants(LinearlyReductiveAction,ZZ):
    invariants_lpLinearlyReductiveAction_cmZZ_rp, or *note
    invariants(LinearlyReductiveAction,List):
    invariants_lpLinearlyReductiveAction_cmZZ_rp,: computes a basis for graded
    component of the invariant ring of a linearly reductive group action

Caveat
======

Some optional inputs are only relevant to certain use cases of this method.
Please consult the documentation pages for the different cases to learn which
optional inputs are used.

See also
========

  * *note invariantRing: invariantRing, -- the ring of invariants of a group
    action
  * *note isInvariant: isInvariant, -- check whether a polynomial is invariant
    under a group action

Ways to use invariants:
=======================

  * *note invariants(DiagonalAction): invariants_lpDiagonalAction_rp, --
    computes the generating invariants of a group action
  * *note invariants(FiniteGroupAction): invariants_lpFiniteGroupAction_rp, --
    computes the generating invariants of a group action
  * "invariants(FiniteGroupAction,List)" -- see *note
    invariants(FiniteGroupAction,ZZ): invariants_lpFiniteGroupAction_cmZZ_rp,
    -- basis for graded component of invariant ring
  * *note invariants(FiniteGroupAction,ZZ):
    invariants_lpFiniteGroupAction_cmZZ_rp, -- basis for graded component of
    invariant ring
  * *note invariants(LinearlyReductiveAction):
    invariants_lpLinearlyReductiveAction_rp, -- invariant generators of Hilbert
    ideal
  * "invariants(LinearlyReductiveAction,List)" -- see *note
    invariants(LinearlyReductiveAction,ZZ):
    invariants_lpLinearlyReductiveAction_cmZZ_rp, -- basis for graded component
    of invariant ring
  * *note invariants(LinearlyReductiveAction,ZZ):
    invariants_lpLinearlyReductiveAction_cmZZ_rp, -- basis for graded component
    of invariant ring

