invariants(...,SubringLimit=>...) -- GB option for invariants
*************************************************************

Description
===========

The computation of invariants of linearly reductive group actions requires the
use of Gröbner bases. These options allow partial control over the computation
performed by *note invariants(LinearlyReductiveAction):
invariants_lpLinearlyReductiveAction_rp, and *note
hilbertIdeal(LinearlyReductiveAction): hilbertIdeal,, allowing to terminate the
computation after a certain number of invariants are obtained. For more
information, see *note gb: (Macaulay2Doc)gb,.

