Description
===========

This function is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,

When called on a finite group action and a (multi)degree, it computes an
additive basis for the invariants of the action in the given degree.

This function uses an implementation of the Linear Algebra Method described in
§3.1.1 of

  * Derksen, H. & Kemper, G. (2015).Computational Invariant Theory. Heidelberg:
    Springer.

For example, consider the following action of a dihedral group.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K=toField(QQ[a]/(a^2+a+1));                         |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = K[x,y]                                          |
|                                                         |
|o2 = R                                                   |
|                                                         |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A=matrix{{a,0},{0,a^2}};                            |
|                                                         |
|             2      2                                    |
|o3 : Matrix K  <-- K                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : B=sub(matrix{{0,1},{1,0}},K);                       |
|                                                         |
|             2      2                                    |
|o4 : Matrix K  <-- K                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D6=finiteAction({A,B},R)                            |
|                                                         |
|o5 = R <- <| a 0    |, | 0 1 |>                          |
|           | 0 -a-1 |  | 1 0 |                           |
|                                                         |
|o5 : FiniteGroupAction                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : invariants(D6,20)                                   |
|                                                         |
|       10 10   13 7    7 13   16 4    4 16   19       19 |
|o6 = {x  y  , x  y  + x y  , x  y  + x y  , x  y + x*y  }|
|                                                         |
|o6 : List                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

It is important to note that this implementation uses the group generators
provided by the user, which can be recovered using *note
generators(FiniteGroupAction): generators_lpFiniteGroupAction_rp,. To improve
efficiency the user should provide a generating set for the group that is as
small as possible.

See also
========

  * *note invariantRing: invariantRing, -- the ring of invariants of a group
    action
  * *note isInvariant: isInvariant, -- check whether a polynomial is invariant
    under a group action
  * *note finiteAction: finiteAction, -- the group action generated by a list
    of matrices

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "invariants(FiniteGroupAction,List)"
  * *note invariants(FiniteGroupAction,ZZ):
    invariants_lpFiniteGroupAction_cmZZ_rp, -- basis for graded component of
    invariant ring
