invariants(LinearlyReductiveAction,ZZ) -- basis for graded component of invariant ring
**************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note invariants: invariants,
  * Usage: 
        invariants(V,d)
  * Inputs:
      * V, an instance of the type *note LinearlyReductiveAction:
        LinearlyReductiveAction,
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a degree or multidegree
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note DegreeBound: invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeBound=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value infinity, degree bound for invariants of finite
        groups
      * *note DegreeLimit: invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value {}, GB option for invariants
      * *note Strategy: invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value "Default", choose the strategy for computing
        invariants
      * *note SubringLimit: invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSubringLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value infinity, GB option for invariants
      * *note UseCoefficientRing:
        invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmUseCoefficientRing=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, option to compute invariants over the given
        coefficient ring
      * *note UsePolyhedra: invariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmUsePolyhedra=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value false, use Polyhedra package for invariants of
        tori
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, an additive basis for a graded
        component of the ring of invariants

Description
===========

This function is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,

When called on a linearly reductive group action and a (multi)degree, it
computes an additive basis for the invariants of the action in the given
degree.

This function uses an implementation of Algorithm 4.5.1 in:

  * Derksen, H. & Kemper, G. (2015).Computational Invariant Theory. Heidelberg:
    Springer.

The following example examines the action of the special linear group of degree
2 on the space of binary quadrics. There is a single invariant of degree 2 but
no invariant of degree 3.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[a,b,c,d]                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a*d - b*c - 1)                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = ideal(- b*c + a*d - 1)                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of S                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A = S[u,v]                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = A                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M = transpose (map(S,A)) last coefficients                              |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = | a2 2ab   b2 |                                                         |
|     | ac bc+ad bd |                                                         |
|     | c2 2cd   d2 |                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|             3      3                                                        |
|o4 : Matrix S  <-- S                                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|sub(basis(2,A),{u=>a*u+b*v,v=>c*u+d*v})                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = QQ[x_1..x_3]                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : V = linearlyReductiveAction(I,M,R)                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = R <- S/ideal(- b*c + a*d - 1) via                                       |
|                                                                             |
|     | a2 2ab   b2 |                                                         |
|     | ac bc+ad bd |                                                         |
|     | c2 2cd   d2 |                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : LinearlyReductiveAction                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : invariants(V,2)                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|       2                                                                     |
|o7 = {x  - 4x x }                                                            |
|       2     1 3                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : invariants(V,3)                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = {}                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o8 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note invariantRing: invariantRing, -- the ring of invariants of a group
    action
  * *note isInvariant: isInvariant, -- check whether a polynomial is invariant
    under a group action
  * *note linearlyReductiveAction: linearlyReductiveAction, -- Linearly
    reductive group action

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "invariants(LinearlyReductiveAction,List)"
  * *note invariants(LinearlyReductiveAction,ZZ):
    invariants_lpLinearlyReductiveAction_cmZZ_rp, -- basis for graded component
    of invariant ring
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

