File: InvariantRing.info, Node: LinearlyReductiveAction, Next: linearlyReductiveAction, Prev: isInvariant, Up: Top

LinearlyReductiveAction -- the class of all (non finite, non toric) linearly reductive group actions
****************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

This class is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,.

LinearlyReductiveAction is the class of all linearly reductive group actions on
(quotients of) polynomial rings for the        purpose of computing invariants.
It is created using *note linearlyReductiveAction: linearlyReductiveAction,.
This class should not be used for actions of tori or finite groups, as its
methods for computing invariants are in general less efficient than specialized
methods for the classes *note FiniteGroupAction: FiniteGroupAction,, and *note
DiagonalAction: DiagonalAction,.

Functions and methods returning an object of class LinearlyReductiveAction:
===========================================================================

  * "linearlyReductiveAction(Ideal,Matrix,PolynomialRing)" -- see *note
    linearlyReductiveAction: linearlyReductiveAction, -- Linearly reductive
    group action
  * "linearlyReductiveAction(Ideal,Matrix,QuotientRing)" -- see *note
    linearlyReductiveAction: linearlyReductiveAction, -- Linearly reductive
    group action

Methods that use an object of class LinearlyReductiveAction:
============================================================

  * "actionMatrix(LinearlyReductiveAction)" -- see *note actionMatrix:
    actionMatrix, -- matrix of a linearly reductive action
  * "groupIdeal(LinearlyReductiveAction)" -- see *note groupIdeal: groupIdeal,
    -- ideal defining a linearly reductive group
