molienSeries -- computes the Molien (Hilbert) series of the invariant ring of a finite group
********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        molienSeries G
  * Inputs:
      * G, an instance of the type *note FiniteGroupAction: FiniteGroupAction,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note divide expression: (Macaulay2Doc)Divide,, the Molien series of
        the invariant ring of G as a rational function

Description
===========

This function is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,.

The example below computes the Molien series for the dihedral group with 6
elements. K is the field obtained by adjoining a primitive third root of unity
to *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : K=toField(QQ[a]/(a^2+a+1));     |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : A=matrix{{a,0},{0,a^2}};        |
|                                     |
|             2      2                |
|o2 : Matrix K  <-- K                 |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : B=sub(matrix{{0,1},{1,0}},K);   |
|                                     |
|             2      2                |
|o3 : Matrix K  <-- K                 |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : D6=finiteAction({A,B},K[x,y])   |
|                                     |
|o4 = K[x..y] <- <| a 0    |, | 0 1 |>|
|                 | 0 -a-1 |  | 1 0 | |
|                                     |
|o4 : FiniteGroupAction               |
+-------------------------------------+
|i5 : molienSeries D6                 |
|                                     |
|             1                       |
|o5 = ----------------                |
|           2       3                 |
|     (1 - T )(1 - T )                |
|                                     |
|o5 : Expression of class Divide      |
+-------------------------------------+

Ways to use molienSeries:
=========================

  * "molienSeries(FiniteGroupAction)"

