numgens(DiagonalAction) -- number of generators of the finite part of a diagonal group
**************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note numgens: (Macaulay2Doc)numgens,
  * Usage: 
        numgens D
  * Inputs:
      * D, an instance of the type *note DiagonalAction: DiagonalAction,, the
        action of a diagonal group
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of generators of the
        group

Description
===========

This function is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,. 

Writing the diagonal group acting on the polynomial ring $k[x_1,\dots,x_n]$ as
$(k^*)^r \times \mathbb{Z}/d_1 \times \cdots \times \mathbb{Z}/d_g$, this
function returns g.

Here is an example of a product of two cyclic groups of order 3 acting on a
polynomial ring in 3 variables.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_1..x_3]           |
|                                |
|o1 = R                          |
|                                |
|o1 : PolynomialRing             |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : d = {3,3}                  |
|                                |
|o2 = {3, 3}                     |
|                                |
|o2 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : W = matrix{{1,0,1},{0,1,1}}|
|                                |
|o3 = | 1 0 1 |                  |
|     | 0 1 1 |                  |
|                                |
|              2       3         |
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ          |
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : A = diagonalAction(W, d, R)|
|                                |
|o4 = R <- ZZ/3 x ZZ/3 via       |
|                                |
|     | 1 0 1 |                  |
|     | 0 1 1 |                  |
|                                |
|o4 : DiagonalAction             |
+--------------------------------+
|i5 : numgens A                  |
|                                |
|o5 = 2                          |
+--------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note numgens(DiagonalAction): numgens_lpDiagonalAction_rp, -- number of
    generators of the finite part of a diagonal group
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

