primaryInvariants -- computes a list of primary invariants for the invariant ring of a finite group
***************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        primaryInvariants G
  * Inputs:
      * G, an instance of the type *note FiniteGroupAction: FiniteGroupAction,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Dade: primaryInvariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDade=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, an optional argument for primaryInvariants
        determining whether to use the Dade algorithm
      * *note DegreeVector: primaryInvariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeVector=>_pd_
        pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value 0, an optional argument for
        primaryInvariants that finds invariants of certain degrees
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,,  consisting of a homogeneous system
        of parameters (hsop) for the invariant ring of the group action

Description
===========

There are two algorithms implemented in *note primaryInvariants:
primaryInvariants,. The default algorithm (corresponding to the optional
argument *note Dade: primaryInvariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDade=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, taking
the value *note false: (Macaulay2Doc)false,) currently only works with
polynomial rings over fields of characteristic zero. The second is the Dade
algorithm, corresponding to the optional argument *note Dade:
primaryInvariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDade=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, taking the value *note
true: (Macaulay2Doc)true,. This algorithm can calculate an hsop over finite
fields, so long as the field is sufficiently large. See *note hsop algorithms:
hsop algorithms, for a discussion comparing the two algorithms.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A=matrix{{0,1,0},{0,0,1},{1,0,0}};        |
|                                               |
|              3       3                        |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : B=matrix{{0,1,0},{1,0,0},{0,0,1}};        |
|                                               |
|              3       3                        |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S3=finiteAction({A,B},QQ[x,y,z])          |
|                                               |
|o3 = QQ[x..z] <- <| 0 1 0 |, | 0 1 0 |>        |
|                  | 0 0 1 |  | 1 0 0 |         |
|                  | 1 0 0 |  | 0 0 1 |         |
|                                               |
|o3 : FiniteGroupAction                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : primaryInvariants S3                      |
|                                               |
|                                   3    3    3 |
|o4 = {x + y + z, x*y + x*z + y*z, x  + y  + z }|
|                                               |
|o4 : List                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------+

                                   S3
Below, the invariant ring QQ[x,y,z]   is calculated with K being the field with
101 elements.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : K=GF(101)                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = K                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : GaloisField                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : S3=finiteAction({A,B},K[x,y,z])                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = K[x..z] <- <| 0 1 0 |, | 0 1 0 |>                                       |
|                 | 0 0 1 |  | 1 0 0 |                                        |
|                 | 1 0 0 |  | 0 0 1 |                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : FiniteGroupAction                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : primaryInvariants(S3,Dade=>true)                                        |
|                                                                             |
|           6      5       4 2      3 3      2 4        5      6      5       |
|o7 = {- 45x  - 28x y - 45x y  - 42x y  - 45x y  - 28x*y  - 45y  - 28x z +    |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        4         3 2       2 3         4       5       4 2      3   2       |
|     11x y*z + 23x y z + 23x y z + 11x*y z - 28y z - 45x z  + 23x y*z  +     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        2 2 2        3 2      4 2      3 3      2   3        2 3      3 3    |
|     18x y z  + 23x*y z  - 45y z  - 42x z  + 23x y*z  + 23x*y z  - 42y z  -  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        2 4          4      2 4        5        5      6    6      5         |
|     45x z  + 11x*y*z  - 45y z  - 28x*z  - 28y*z  - 45z , 9x  + 32x y +      |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        4 2      3 3      2 4        5     6      5       4         3 2      |
|     13x y  - 21x y  + 13x y  + 32x*y  + 9y  + 32x z + 48x y*z + 14x y z +   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        2 3         4       5       4 2      3   2      2 2 2        3 2     |
|     14x y z + 48x*y z + 32y z + 13x z  + 14x y*z  - 33x y z  + 14x*y z  +   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        4 2      3 3      2   3        2 3      3 3      2 4          4      |
|     13y z  - 21x z  + 14x y*z  + 14x*y z  - 21y z  + 13x z  + 48x*y*z  +    |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        2 4        5        5     6     6      5       4 2      2 4        5 |
|     13y z  + 32x*z  + 32y*z  + 9z , 13x  - 43x y + 45x y  + 45x y  - 43x*y  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|          6      5       4         3 2       2 3         4       5       4 2 |
|     + 13y  - 43x z - 23x y*z - 39x y z - 39x y z - 23x*y z - 43y z + 45x z  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|          3   2      2 2 2        3 2      4 2      2   3        2 3      2 4|
|     - 39x y*z  + 29x y z  - 39x*y z  + 45y z  - 39x y*z  - 39x*y z  + 45x z |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|              4      2 4        5        5      6                            |
|     - 23x*y*z  + 45y z  - 43x*z  - 43y*z  + 13z }                           |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This function is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,.

Caveat
======

                                                                           
Currently users can only use *note primaryInvariants: primaryInvariants, to
                                                                             
calculate a hsop for the invariant ring over a finite field by using the Dade
                                                                      
algorithm. Users should enter the finite field as a *note GaloisField:
                                                                    
(Macaulay2Doc)GaloisField, or a quotient field of the form *note ZZ:
                                                                       
(Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,/p and are advised to ensure that the ground field has
                            n-1
cardinality greater than |G|   , where n is the number of variables in the
polynomial ring . Using a ground field smaller than this runs the risk of the
algorithm getting stuck in an infinite loop; *note primaryInvariants:
primaryInvariants, displays a warning message asking the user whether they wish
to continue with the computation in this case. See *note hsop algorithms: hsop
algorithms, for a discussion on the Dade algorithm.

Ways to use primaryInvariants:
==============================

  * "primaryInvariants(FiniteGroupAction)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note primaryInvariants: primaryInvariants, is a *note method
function with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

