rank(DiagonalAction) -- of a diagonal action
********************************************

  * Function: *note rank: (Macaulay2Doc)rank,
  * Usage: 
        rank D
  * Inputs:
      * D, an instance of the type *note DiagonalAction: DiagonalAction,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the rank of the torus factor of a
        diagonal action

Description
===========

This function is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,. 

Use this function to recover the rank of the torus factor of a diagonal action.

The following example defines an action of a two-dimensional torus on a
polynomial ring in four variables.

+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_1..x_4]                  |
|                                       |
|o1 = R                                 |
|                                       |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                    |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : W = matrix{{0,1,-1,1},{1,0,-1,-1}}|
|                                       |
|o2 = | 0 1 -1 1  |                     |
|     | 1 0 -1 -1 |                     |
|                                       |
|              2       4                |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                 |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : T = diagonalAction(W, R)          |
|                                       |
|             * 2                       |
|o3 = R <- (QQ )  via                   |
|                                       |
|     | 0 1 -1 1  |                     |
|     | 1 0 -1 -1 |                     |
|                                       |
|o3 : DiagonalAction                    |
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : rank T                            |
|                                       |
|o4 = 2                                 |
+---------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note DiagonalAction: DiagonalAction, -- the class of all diagonal actions
  * *note diagonalAction: diagonalAction, -- diagonal group action via weights

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note rank(DiagonalAction): rank_lpDiagonalAction_rp, -- of a diagonal
    action
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

