RingOfInvariants -- the class of the rings of invariants under the action of a finite group, an Abelian group or a linearly reductive group
*******************************************************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

This class is provided by the package *note InvariantRing: Top,.

RingOfInvariants is the class of rings of invariants when a finite group, an
Abelian group or a linearly reductive group acts on a polynomial ring.

Functions and methods returning an object of class RingOfInvariants:
====================================================================

  * "invariantRing(GroupAction)" -- see *note invariantRing: invariantRing, --
    the ring of invariants of a group action
  * "PolynomialRing ^ GroupAction" -- see *note invariantRing: invariantRing,
    -- the ring of invariants of a group action
  * "QuotientRing ^ LinearlyReductiveAction" -- see *note invariantRing:
    invariantRing, -- the ring of invariants of a group action

Methods that use an object of class RingOfInvariants:
=====================================================

  * "action(RingOfInvariants)" -- see *note action: action, -- the group action
    that produced a ring of invariants
  * *note ambient(RingOfInvariants): ambient_lpRingOfInvariants_rp, -- the
    ambient polynomial ring where the group acted upon
  * "definingIdeal(RingOfInvariants)" -- see *note definingIdeal:
    definingIdeal, -- presentation of a ring of invariants as polynomial ring
    modulo the defining ideal
  * *note generators(RingOfInvariants): generators_lpRingOfInvariants_rp, --
    the generators for a ring of invariants
  * *note hilbertSeries(RingOfInvariants): hilbertSeries_lpRingOfInvariants_rp,
    -- Hilbert series of the invariant ring
  * *note net(RingOfInvariants): net_lpRingOfInvariants_rp, -- format for
    printing, as a net
  * *note texMath(RingOfInvariants): texMath_lpRingOfInvariants_rp, -- format
    for printing, as TeX strings

For the programmer
==================

The object *note RingOfInvariants: RingOfInvariants, is a *note type:
(Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with ancestor classes *note HashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, < *note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

