secondaryInvariants(...,PrintDegreePolynomial=>...) -- an optional argument for secondaryInvariants that determines the printing of an informative polynomial
*************************************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        secondaryInvariants(P,G)
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of primary invariants in n
                                                                               
        variables f ,...,f  for the invariant ring of G defined over a field K
                   1      n
        of characteristic zero
      * G, an instance of the type *note FiniteGroupAction: FiniteGroupAction,
  * Outputs:
                                                                               
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list S of secondary invariants for
                                                                               
                                         G
        the invariant ring R=K[x ,...,x ]  of G that makes R into a free
                                1      n                                
        K[f ,...,f ]-module with basis S
           1      n

Description
===========

                            
*note PrintDegreePolynomial:
                            
                                                                              
secondaryInvariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmPrintDegreePolynomial=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, takes a
                                                                              
                                                                      
*note Boolean: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean, value and is set to *note false:
                                                                      
                                                            
(Macaulay2Doc)false, by default. If it is set to *note true:
                                                            
                                                                              
(Macaulay2Doc)true,, then *note secondaryInvariants: secondaryInvariants, will
                                                                              
                                                                            
print a polynomial in the variable T. This polynomial encodes the degrees of
                                                                            
                                                                              
the secondary invariants (given by the exponents of T appearing in it) and the
                                                                              
                                                                        
number of secondary invariants of a given degree (the coefficient of the
                                                                        
                                                             
corresponding term in the polynomial). Specifically, if *note
                                                             
                                                                         
secondaryInvariants: secondaryInvariants, takes as input a set of primary
                                                                         
                                                       G                     
invariants of degrees d ,...,d  for an invariant ring S  of a finite group G,
                       1      n
       G                                           G            
and H(S ,T)denotes the Molien (Hilbert) series of S , then *note
                                                                     
secondaryInvariants: secondaryInvariants, will compute the polynomial
   G        d           d
H(S ,T)*(1-T 1)*...*(1-T n).

The example below computes the secondary invariants for the dihedral group with
6 elements, given a set of primary invariants P. The optional argument *note
PrintDegreePolynomial: secondaryInvariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmPrintDegreePolynomial
=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, is set to *note true: (Macaulay2Doc)true, in order to see which
degrees the secondary invariants should have.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K=toField(QQ[a]/(a^2+a+1));                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R=K[x,y];                                            |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A=matrix{{a,0},{0,a^2}};                             |
|                                                          |
|             2      2                                     |
|o3 : Matrix K  <-- K                                      |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : B=sub(matrix{{0,1},{1,0}},K);                        |
|                                                          |
|             2      2                                     |
|o4 : Matrix K  <-- K                                      |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D6=finiteAction({A,B},R)                             |
|                                                          |
|o5 = R <- <| a 0    |, | 0 1 |>                           |
|           | 0 -a-1 |  | 1 0 |                            |
|                                                          |
|o5 : FiniteGroupAction                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : P={x^3+y^3,-(x^3-y^3)^2};                            |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : secondaryInvariants(P,D6,PrintDegreePolynomial=>true)|
| 4    2                                                   |
|t  + t  + 1                                               |
|                                                          |
|               2 2                                        |
|o7 = {1, x*y, x y }                                       |
|                                                          |
|o7 : List                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Currently, a user needs to ensure that the all primary invariants are defined
with coefficients in a ring that Macaulay2 recognises as a characteristic zero
field (see *note toField: (Macaulay2Doc)toField_lpRing_rp, for a way to do
this).

Functions with optional argument named PrintDegreePolynomial:
=============================================================

  * "hironakaDecomposition(...,PrintDegreePolynomial=>...)"
  * *note secondaryInvariants(...,PrintDegreePolynomial=>...):
    secondaryInvariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmPrintDegreePolynomial=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, --
    an optional argument for secondaryInvariants that determines the printing
    of an informative polynomial

Further information
===================

  * Default value: *note false: (Macaulay2Doc)false,
  * Function: *note secondaryInvariants: secondaryInvariants, -- computes
    secondary invariants for the invariant ring of a finite group
  * Option key: *note PrintDegreePolynomial:
    secondaryInvariants_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmPrintDegreePolynomial=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, --
    an optional argument for secondaryInvariants that determines the printing
    of an informative polynomial
